Question:
A tower brace is the hypotenuse of length 41 ft, and one leg is 9 ft. What is the other leg?
{
~A. 32 ft#Subtracting side lengths ignores the squared relationship.
=B. 40 ft#Use b^2 = 41^2 - 9^2; the missing leg is 40 ft.
